Subject: allow EXT_FINCOM_IGNORED to be overridden by the build

lwext4 hard-codes which INCOMPAT feature bits it will tolerate on an otherwise
supported volume. We need to add EXT4_FINCOM_BG_USE_META_CSUM (metadata_csum_seed,
0x2000), which modern mke2fs enables by default, and which is safe to ignore
precisely when the stored seed still matches the UUID-derived one -- a condition
the bridge verifies in ext4b_probe() before it ever calls ext4_mount().

Adding an #ifndef guard lets the build supply the value instead of us carrying a
divergent copy of the macro. Upstreamable as-is.

diff --git a/include/ext4_types.h b/include/ext4_types.h
index c9cdd34..7bb482a 100644
--- a/include/ext4_types.h
+++ b/include/ext4_types.h
@@ -295,8 +295,10 @@ struct ext4_sblock {
  *           (probably won't be ever...)
  * MMP - multi-mout protection (impossible scenario)
  * */
+#ifndef EXT_FINCOM_IGNORED
 #define EXT_FINCOM_IGNORED                                 \
 	EXT4_FINCOM_RECOVER | EXT4_FINCOM_MMP
+#endif
 
 #if 0
 /*TODO: Features incompatible to implement*/
